 75CU c  {+75}Cu produced and identified in thermal neutron fission of {+235}U: 
 75CU2c  1985Re01, 1987Ar21, 1990Be13, 1991Kr15                                 
 75CU d  2002Kr13 (also 2002Kr10): {+238}Pu(p,F), E=30 MeV; measured yield      
 75CU2d  of {+75}Cu                                                             
 75CU c  2013Pe03: {+75}Cu was produced following the                           
 75CU2c  fragmentation of {+86}Kr (60.4 MeV/nucleon) beam on Be;                
 75CU3c  B|r-|DE-tof technique was applied using LISE2000                       
 75CU4c  spectrometer at GANIL to identify the fragments. Si and HPGe           
 75CU5c  detectors used to measure particle and |g spectra, respectively.       
 75CU6c  Deduced isomers, half-lives, and level scheme. A previous very         
 75CU7c  similar experiment of the same group is presented in 2010Da06          
 75CU8c  and 1999DaZQ.                                                          
 75CU c  2010Vi07, 2009Fl03: {+75}Cu was produced at ISOLDE-CERN facility by    
 75CU2c  1 GeV proton induced fission of uranium carbide target. Resonance      
 75CU3c  Ionization laser ion source (RILIS) used to laser ionize the atoms     
 75CU4c  followed by high-resolution isotope separation (HRS) and ISCOOL Paul   
 75CU5c  trap. Measured hyperfine structure. Deduced spin, magnetic dipole      
 75CU6c  moment and electric quadrupole moment of the ground state. Collinear   
 75CU7c  and in-source laser spectroscopic technique. Comparison with           
 75CU8c  large-scale shell-model calculations using {+56}Ni core.               
 75CU d  2009Gr06: nothing on {+75}Cu, except perhaps production                
 75CU2d  of isotope at Holifield, ORNL facility.                                
 75CU c  2011Il01: {+75}Cu beam produced from fission of {+238}U                
 75CU2c  (using UC{-x} target with protons at Holifield Radioactive Ion beam    
 75CU3c  facility). Isotopic half-life measured from decay curves of 8 |g rays  
 75CU4c  from decay of {+75}Cu                                                  
 75CU c  2012Ka36: {+75}Cu isomers produced in {+9}Be({+238}U,X) at             
 75CU2c  345 MeV/nucleon using BigRIPS separator at RIKEN facility. Measured    
 75CU3c  delayed |g rays and isomer half-life. Total of 5.4|*10{+5} {+75}Cu     
 75CU4c  fragments detected                                                     
 75CU c  Mass measurement (Penning-trap system): 2007Ra27, 2005Gu36             
 75CU c  Structure calculations: 2010Si11 (levels, J, |p, |m), 2005Bo19         
 75CU2c  (half-life and delayed-neutron emission probability), 2005Li54         
 75CU3c  (calculated 5/2- and 3/2- levels), 2004Sm03 (levels, shell model),     
 75CU4c  2012Sr02, 2012Sr03 (shell model).                                      
 75CU d  {+76}Ni, in principle, can decay by |b-delayed neutron emission to     
 75CU2d  {+75}Cu, but no experimental information is available.                 
